    "text": "By John Ghost ,\n1 days ago Coupeville’s history runs deeper than you’d think. Two hours north of Seattle, a ferry drops you on Whidbey Island and the road leads straight to one of Washington’s oldest towns. Coupeville sits on the shore of Penn Cove, where the Lower Skagit people kept three permanent villages... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
